+# Export acceptance and restart recovery hunt
+
+Checked revision: `817185a6bf680e6aa24432f9b1061e26ed08e1d0`.
+
+## Scope and fault model
+
+Scope: `Queue.submit`, `Queue.work`, constructor recovery, and `Queue.result`
+in [app/export_queue.py](app/export_queue.py), governed by
+[app/export-contract.md](app/export-contract.md). Prioritized harms were
+abandoned accepted work, false acceptance durability, and repeated completed
+work. Stop after these operation and direct recovery cases; no broader app audit.
+
+The contract establishes local SQLite persistence across process termination,
+one worker, sequential requests, restart only after the old worker stops,
+immutable payload per ID, and repeated work calls after transient failures
+cease. Storage loss/corruption and overlapping workers are excluded by that
+contract. The witness uses actual process termination, a temporary local database,
+and the documented post-running-commit hook. No mocked queue or state model.
+
+## Demonstrated defect: accepted jobs become permanently stranded
+
+**High impact:** interruption after the running-state commit abandons accepted
+work, violating “Accepted jobs must eventually produce their result after
+recovery.”
+
+Reachable trace:
+
+1. `submit("job", "payload")` commits a pending job and returns accepted
+   (`app/export_queue.py:21–25`).
+2. `work` commits `state = 'running'` (`:33–34`). Its documented hook then
+   terminates the child with `os._exit(73)`, before output starts.
+3. A fresh process opens the same database. Constructor calls `recover`, but
+   it does nothing (`:15–19`). The job remains running without a result.
+4. Repeated `work` calls select only pending jobs (`:28–32`), return false,
+   and never produce this job's result.
+
+This is permanent under allowed recovery, rather than a transient delay:
+without another pending job, each work call takes the same read-only false
+branch; restart has no recovery mutation. Even a same-ID submission retry uses
+`INSERT OR IGNORE`, so cannot restore the obligation. A healthy environment and
+arbitrarily many retries cannot change this closed state.
+
+Fix direction: reconstruct unfinished running obligations at restart, or make
+them eligible for retry under the single-worker contract. Preserve the atomic
+result insertion/done transition and completed-job behavior. No repair applied.
+
+## Executed evidence and coverage
+
+Command: `python3 -B tests/hunt_witness.py` using Python 3.9.6.
+Observed exit status: **1**, with:
+
+```text
+PASS: pending restart, completion and completed retry
+FAIL: running: accepted job has no result after restart and five work calls (initial persisted state=running)
+```
+
+[tests/hunt_witness.py](tests/hunt_witness.py) exits nonzero on violated
+assertions and zero when both scenarios satisfy the contract. Each scenario
+uses a separate database; subprocess termination is checked before restart.
+Assertions inspect real results, and the passing case additionally checks
+completed state behavior across a second restart and same-payload resubmission.
+Scratch databases are removed automatically. This is a direct executable
+counterexample and control case, not a generated search or formal proof.
+
+| Case | Coverage and outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| Accepted pending job, termination before work | Executed: survives restart and completes |
+| Termination after running commit, before output | Executed: stranded job, missing result |
+| Completed job after restart; same-ID/same-payload retry | Executed in pending control: result preserved, no new work |
+| Output insert and done update atomicity | Code inspection: both in one SQLite transaction; no process kill inside transaction executed |
+| Transient error after running commit | Code inspection: same stranding mechanism if output transaction fails and rolls back; no I/O fault injection executed |
+| Submit before commit | Code inspection only: no successful acceptance returned before transaction exit |
+
+No counterexample found in the executed control; that is not a guarantee of bug
+absence. Other commit boundaries were not exhaustively fault-injected. SQLite
+transaction durability is taken from the supplied contract; no pinned SQLite
+source or storage implementation audit was performed. No missing tool blocked
+the selected checks.
+
+## Records and preservation
+
+Discovery covered root `specs/`, app paths and references to queue/recovery and
+record IDs. No narrower specs directory or queue consumer was found. Read the
+root architecture, gate, requirement, payload spec, and single-writer claim as
+context. The local-only gate is respected by temporary local databases. The
+claim concerns writes under `data/`; this witness does not write there and
+neither verifies nor changes that claim. Claim proof/verification artifacts
+were not used or modified. Unrelated note export and import behavior are outside
+this hunt. Product code, governing records, and existing evidence are preserved.
